# The app project publishes the whole repository, so the marketing site is
# reachable at sproutevergreen.app/site/ as well as at its own domain. One
# page on two URLs is a page that gets indexed twice and updated once.
/site/*  https://sproutevergreen.com/:splat  301

# The web app is retired: sproutevergreen.app's front door goes to the
# marketing site, which hands the reader to the stores. Only "/" moves. The
# app's files stay published under it: native/copy-web.js builds the store
# apps from this same tree (it copies css, js, img and three files, never
# this one), the planner preview is planned to be served from them, and
# every old link to sproutevergreen.app, the reels' outro among them, still
# lands somewhere. 302 rather than 301, so no browser remembers it for good
# if the front door is ever given back to something.
/  https://sproutevergreen.com/  302
